<h2 class="bde-heading-506-128 bde-heading">
Why Do the Thunder Pay Kenrich Williams $5m?
</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-506-129 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-506-145 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-506-158 bde-f-text">
<p>Williams is paid <strong>$5m</strong> because Oklahoma City declined a more expensive option year and re-signed him cheaper on the same day, which a club can do when it holds Bird rights.</p>
<ul>
<li>He went undrafted in 2018 and his first contract guaranteed him <strong>$50k</strong>.</li>
<li>He arrived at Oklahoma City in a sign-and-trade in 2020.</li>
<li>The club extended him in 2022 for <strong>$27.17m</strong> across four seasons.</li>
<li>It declined the option on this season on June 29, 2026 and signed this deal instead.</li>
<li>The new contract carries up to <strong>$500k</strong> in incentives.</li>
</ul>
<p>He is one of three players named Williams on the Oklahoma City payroll.</p>

