<script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://nbasalaries.com/players/kenrich-williams/#faq","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://nbasalaries.com/players/kenrich-williams/"},"mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What Is Kenrich Williams’s Salary in 2026-27?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Williams earns $5m in 2026-27, tenth at Oklahoma City on a new one-year contract. It falls from $7.16m last season. His career earnings come to $33.26m across nine seasons. The salary is 2.33% of the club’s $214.28m payroll."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What’s Next for Kenrich Williams Beyond 2026?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The contract covers this season only and all of it is guaranteed. He reaches free agency again in 2027 at 32."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How Much Does Kenrich Williams Earn Over Time?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A $5m season is hard to picture, so here's what it comes to over smaller stretches of time."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"When Does Kenrich Williams’s Contract Expire?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Williams signed a one-year contract worth $5m with Oklahoma City in 2026 under Bird rights, all of it guaranteed, with up to $500k in incentives on top. The club had declined the final option year of his extension the same day. He reaches free agency again in 2027 at 32."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What Is Kenrich Williams’s Net Worth?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Williams’s net worth is estimated at around $13.3m, taken from his $33.26m in career earnings. No outlet publishes a figure for him. He played four seasons at TCU and went undrafted in 2018. New Orleans signed him that summer, at 23."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why Do the Thunder Pay Kenrich Williams $5m?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Williams is paid $5m because Oklahoma City declined a more expensive option year and re-signed him cheaper on the same day, which a club can do when it holds Bird rights. He is one of three players named Williams on the Oklahoma City payroll."}}]}</script>
